  "notes": {
    "namespaces-not-folders": "Namespaces deliberately do not follow folders: Models/User.cs is Shop.Domain, Legacy/User.cs is Legacy.Accounts, Utils/Formatting.cs is Shop.Text, Mapping/Mappers.cs is Shop.Mapping, Extensions/ is Shop.Domain, src/Shop.App is Shop.Cli.",
    "two-users-using": "Two classes named User live in two User.cs files. Mappers.cs is in Shop.Mapping with `using Legacy.Accounts;` and no route to Shop.Domain.User by simple name, so `User` there is Legacy.Accounts.User (Legacy/User.cs) and `legacy.Display()` is its Display.",
    "enclosing-namespace-wins": "UserService.cs has `using Legacy.Accounts;` yet sits in namespace Shop.Domain.Services. C# name lookup walks the enclosing namespaces (Shop.Domain.Services, then Shop.Domain) before it reaches the compilation unit's using directives, so `User` is Shop.Domain.User (Models/User.cs). A resolver that trusts the using directive picks the wrong file.",
    "dynamic": "`account` is `dynamic`: the call is bound at run time to whatever object is passed. Both User classes have Display, so both files are plausible. This is the only C# call here whose target the compiler does not fix; the two-User.cs calls above are statically unambiguous for the compiler, just not from file names.",
    "global-using": "`global using Shop.Text;` (one GlobalUsings.cs per project, each applies to its own project) makes Formatting visible without a per-file using.",
    "block-namespace": "AuditLog.cs uses a block namespace `namespace Shop.Domain.Services { ... }`; UserService.cs uses the file-scoped form of the same namespace. Same namespace, no using needed.",
    "extension-method": "`user.Initials()` is the extension method UserExtensions.Initials (namespace Shop.Domain, found by walking enclosing namespaces from Shop.Domain.Services). The IMPORTS row records the dependency on UserExtensions.cs even though the type name is never written.",
    "partial-class": "Order is partial over Order.cs and Order.Pricing.cs. Subtotal/Tax are declared only in Order.Pricing.cs, AddLine/Total only in Order.cs; a reference to the type Order depends on both files.",
    "class-not-named-after-file": "Mappers.cs declares UserMapper; there is no UserMapper.cs.",
    "using-alias": "`using LegacyUser = Legacy.Accounts.User;` so `LegacyUser.Parse` is Legacy/User.cs.",
    "same-namespace": "Banner is internal in namespace Shop.Cli in the same project as Program.",
    "qualified-name": "`Shop.Domain.User` written fully qualified (constructor only, no call).",
    "bcl-collection": "List<T>.Add / LINQ Sum, FirstOrDefault are BCL; must not link to repo functions.",
    "imports-format": "C# has no file imports: a using directive names a namespace. IMPORTS truth is the file-level dependency the compiler resolves: from_file -> each other in-repo file declaring a type (or extension method) this file references, kind `type-ref`. Using directives alone, with nothing referenced, give no row.",
    "scope": "Constructor invocations (`new UserService()`, `new User(...)`) are not listed as calls. Properties (`_users.Count`, `Name`) are not calls. .csproj/.sln are not source."
  }
}
